James inquired about the scaling law for domino propagation speed, questioning why greater separation \( \lambda \) leads to faster propagation despite seemingly requiring a longer distance to travel. I explained that while this seems counterintuitive, dimensional analysis reveals non-intuitive relationships affecting dynamics. Key points included the potential for greater energy transfer when dominoes fall from larger separations, the impact angle, stability thresholds, and the dimensional focus of the results. Ultimately, I emphasized that the analysis is specific to ideal scenarios and may not account for real-world complexities that could slow down the cascade, suggesting a more comprehensive dynamical model for deeper insights.
